# Walkthrough - Metallic-Glass Aesthetic Refinement

I have upgraded the "liquid glass" effect to a "metallic-glass" look that is cleaner, more aesthetic, and sober, while removing unnecessary UI text elements.

## Changes Made

### 1. Metallic-Glass CSS Upgrade
Refined the `.liquid-glass` class in [globals.css](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/app/globals.css) to achieve a professional, high-end feel:
- **Metallic Sweep**: Replaced the radial light with a **linear sweep highlight** that crosses the card on hover, simulating a polished metallic surface.
- **Chiseled Borders**: Implemented ultra-fine, multi-layered borders to create a "machined" edge look.
- **Sober Colors**: Neutralized the color palette to silver/white tones, keeping the design professional and expensive-looking without distractions.
- **Deep Glass**: Increased the backdrop blur to `20px` for a more substantial glass feel.

### 2. Carousel Refinement
- **Text Removal**: As requested, removed the "DESLICE PARA VER MÁS • PAUSE AL PASAR EL CURSOR" text from the bottom of the services section to maintain a cleaner, more minimalist layout.
- **UI Cleaning**: Removed redundant spacing and empty containers in the [Services.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/components/sections/Services.tsx) component.

### 3. Card Proportions
- Updated the Benefits and Services cards to have more generous padding and a refined corner radius that complements the metallic aesthetic.

